# wp-content/themes/ is bind-mounted as ONE folder so WordPress can see
# everything in a single flat directory, but only YOUR custom themes are
# tracked by git. Everything else (third-party themes, whatever gets
# extracted from init-data/themes*.tar.gz, anything installed from the WP
# admin) is ignored by default.
#
# Convention: every locally-developed theme folder must be prefixed with
# "acme-" (rename to your own project/company prefix, e.g. "acme-" ->
# "yourco-"). That's the ONLY thing that decides whether a theme folder is
# versioned or not - no need to keep editing this file as you add themes.

# 1. Ignore everything in this directory...
*

# 2. ...except this file itself...
!.gitignore

# 3. ...and any custom theme folder matching the prefix (and its contents).
!acme-*/
!acme-*/**
